---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="Refund & Cancellation Policy" description="Shiftify refund and cancellation policy — date changes, cancellations before move day, service failures and refund timelines." canonicalPath="/refund-policy/">
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose-sfx">
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem);letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin-bottom:6px">Refund &amp; cancellation policy</h1>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--color-slate-400)">Last updated: September 2026 · {SITE.tradeName}</p>

    <h2>No booking advance — by design</h2>
    <p>Because we do not charge a booking advance, in most cases a cancellation involves no money moving at all: inform us and the booking stands cancelled. This policy exists because advance-payment fraud is common in this industry, and we want our customers to never fight for their own money back.</p>

    <h2>Rescheduling</h2>
    <p>Date changes up to 48 hours before a local move and 72 hours before an intercity move are free, subject to slot and vehicle availability. Society lift slots are re-booked where required.</p>

    <h2>Payments already made</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Where a stage payment is due under your written quote and has been made for work not yet performed, unused amounts are refundable on cancellation.</li>
      <li>Refunds are processed to the original payment method within 5–7 working days of confirmation.</li>
      <li>Costs actually incurred before cancellation (e.g., survey visits already completed where charged, packing material delivered) may be deducted with documentation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>If we cancel</h2>
    <p>In the rare event we cannot serve a confirmed move, you receive all amounts paid with a written explanation — and we'll tell you as early as we know, never on move morning.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Refunds: {SITE.email} · {SITE.phoneDisplay}. Reference your quote number.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
